  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the 19th-Century San Sebastian Basilica in Manila, Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An engineering marvel made of prefabricated and painted parts manufactured in Europe, San Sebastian is the only all-steel building in the Philippines and one of few all-steel churches in the world. This project supports the continuation of work begun under a previous Ambassadors Fund grant to document and stabilize the building.</narrative>
  </description>
